  "summary_en": "Nevada Revised Statutes Chapter 482A governs testing and operation of autonomous vehicles (SAE J3016 levels 3-5): it requires $5M insurance or a bond for testing, a human operator unless the vehicle can reach a minimal risk condition, crash reporting, and certification. It limits manufacturer liability for third-party conversions, gives the state DMV exclusive authority and sets penalties.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Testing requires $5,000,000 insurance, self-insurance or surety bond",
   "Human operator able to take immediate control is required unless a fully autonomous vehicle can achieve a minimal risk condition",
   "Original manufacturers are not liable for defects caused by third-party conversion or unauthorized modification",
   "Test crashes causing injury or damage above $750 must be reported to the Department within 10 business days",
   "Department has exclusive authority to regulate AV technology and may license certification facilities; local taxes and fees on AVs are prohibited"
  ],
